Audit complete: **FAIL / NOT_LEGIT**.

Although all six claims freshly produced `#Top`, the proof:

- Uses an incorrect exact-decimal model of CPython floats; input `3.7` yields `"A"` in K but `"A-"` in both Python implementations.
- Proves only empty, singleton, and one fixed five-element input—not arbitrary-length lists.

